Acceleration and storage of beam bunches at RHIC use two Radio Frequency (RF) system. One operating at 28 MHz is used to capture the AGS bunches and accelerate to the top energy. The other operating at 197 MHz is used to store the beam, which is transferred from the acceleration RF system. The storage RF system shorten the bunches and store the beam for 10 hours.

