Whether the system is thermalized is one of issues in terms of QGP formation. Both theory and experiment draw attention to this issue. The values of integrated \(v_{2}\) increases when collision centrality decreases. This is because the eccentricity \(\varepsilon\) is the largest for most peripheral collisions. In case of local thermalization, the centrality dependence in \(v_{2}/\varepsilon\) should disappear.

